-- title:
--   Second branch reading of the p-fibre function field
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime, let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p` (the bundle of properness, flatness, integrality and normality data for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full level-$p$ modular function field over $\mathbb Z$, together with its rational and geometric curve models, sections and smooth locus), let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, let $K$ be a fraction field of $O$ and $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ a ring homomorphism. Write $X$ for the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z \to O$, assumed integral, and let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from the function field of $X$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$p$ modular function field. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a perfect algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, $red : A \to k$, `data` a `ModularPolynomialData p` satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (Y^p - X)(Y - X^p) \bmod p$, and $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ the integrality of the two level-raising inclusions from level $1$ to level $p$; let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` for these data at level $N = 1$ and $R$ a `ProlongationTuple` for $P$, so in particular $R$ carries two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` exchanged by the Atkin–Lehner involution, with residue maps into the characteristic-$p$ modular function fields. Assume $\iota_K$ maps $O$ into $A$, and let $to\kappa : O \to k$ satisfy $to\kappa(a) = red(\iota_K(a))$ for all $a \in O$. Let $\xi$ be the image of the generic point of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ under the morphism $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap` $to\kappa$, and consider the local ring $\mathcal O_{X,\xi}$. The hypotheses on $\varphi$ are: it sends the germ at $\xi$ of the global section of $X$ coming from $a \in O$ to the image of $\iota_K(a)$ (hypothesis `hφO`); for every $u \in \mathcal O_{X,\xi}$ the value $\varphi(u)$ lies in the valuation subring `R.R₂.integers` (`hval`); for $u$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,\xi}$ the residue `R.residue₂` of $\varphi(u)$ vanishes (`hloc`); and some $u \in \mathcal O_{X,\xi}$ has $\varphi(u) =$ `jQFun 1 p`, the element $j(q^p)$ (`hj`). Then there is a ring isomorphism $\theta : \mathrm{RatFunc}\,k \to$ `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated over $k$ by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`, which is the identity on the constants $k$, and which satisfies, for every $u \in \mathcal O_{X,\xi}$, that $\theta$ applied to the image of $u$ under the stalk map at the generic point transported by $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ equals `R.residue₂` of $\varphi(u)$.
--
--   This identifies the function field of the branch of the Deligne–Rapoport special fibre at $p$ singled out by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}$ with the level-one modular function field over $k$, in a way compatible with the reading $\varphi$ of the function field of $X$ through the second prolongation of the place-specialisation data. It is used in the comparison of node residues and orders at specialised places, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal), for the second branch.
